# Sublinearity and weak square type for literal selected `Q4` shells

The `Q4` radius-gap shell is generally not positive.  What the crossed
interpolation proof needs is instead its ordinary linearity on an integrable
domain, followed by the triangle inequality, and the elementary Chebyshev
conversion of its literal square-energy estimate to weak type `(2,2)`.

This file supplies exactly those bridges for `q4SelectedKernelTTStarShell`.
